/nodus/oevm/tests/test_mirrors_32
/nodus/oevm/tests/test_fibers
/nodus/oevm/tests/test_fibers_32
/nodus/oevm/tests/test_nlr
/nodus/oevm/tests/test_nlr_32

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runner binary (regenerated by the test harness)
oevm_runner

# Benchmark binary (regenerated by bench.sh)
oevm_bench

# One-off manual build outputs (asan/valgrind/gc-stress variants, ad-hoc images).
# The canonical source map is src/solidified_image.stmap (tracked); these temp
# bases are underscore-prefixed so they don't collide with it.
oevm_img
_*.stmap
/nodus/oevm/src/_*.stmap
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build/
# Per-board build dirs (rung 8): each board keeps its own warm CMake/ninja cache, so
# switching boards no longer forces a ~10-minute pristine rebuild.
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-dk/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-dongle/
# Soft-float dongle variant (Issue-A suspect #2 experiment; see
# review/ISSUE-dongle-usb-openthread.md).
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-dongle-softfloat/
# ESP32 per-model build dirs (run.sh defaults to build-esp32-<MODEL>), the
# throwaway layoutdump app, and the Model B blob — all regenerated by a bake.
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-esp32-*/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/layoutdump/build/
# The Model B bake emits <node>.oimg plus TWO sidecars beside it: <node>.stmap
# (ns_compile_oevm.py writes splitext(out)[0] + ".stmap" for BOTH output
# formats) and <node>.oimg.methods.json (#164's offset->name map, written as
# out + ".methods.json"). All three are regenerated by the bake.
#
# The .methods.json needs its own line: `*.oimg` does not match
# `X.oimg.methods.json`, so the sidecar sat untracked after every build until
# #165's final review. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`, which is the only
# way to tell a live pattern from a shape that silently matches nothing.
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/*.oimg
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/*.oimg.methods.json
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/*.stmap

/nodus/oevm/zephyr/prj_dk_thread_local.conf
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/prj_dongle_thread_local.conf
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/prj_esp32_wifi.local.conf
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/prj_esp32c6_thread.local.conf
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-c6-probe/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-c6-netprobe/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-c6-thread/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-esp32c6-*/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-heapprobe-*/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/layoutdump/build-c6/
# ESP32-S2 / MagTag (run.sh defaults to build-esp32s2-<MODEL>) and its layoutdump run.
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-esp32s2-*/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build-layoutdump-s2/
# The Adafruit MagTag reference drop: an 18 MB vendor PDF plus the CircuitPython
# IL0373 driver zips. Reference material, not source — the IL0373 register map it
# documents belongs in the uc81xx quirks entry when that lands, not here.
# Written as dir/* rather than dir/ so git still descends and the negations below
# take effect: an ignored *directory* is never entered, and a `!` inside one is
# silently dead. The vendor drop stays out; the two source files opt back in by
# name, so anything new here is ignored by default — deliberate (#56).
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/boards/magtag/*
!/nodus/oevm/zephyr/boards/magtag/capture.py
!/nodus/oevm/zephyr/boards/magtag/README.md

# Zephyr build trees — 4.5 GB as of 2026-08-02, never commit. The path-agnostic
# form survives the rete restructure (zephyr/ becomes nodus/oevm/zephyr/); the
# anchored form below is re-rooted to match, kept for the same reason every
# other single-file/single-dir pattern in this section is kept explicit.
**/zephyr/build*/
/nodus/oevm/zephyr/build*/

# Agent scratch: session config and the SDD ledger/briefs. Not repo content.
.claude/
.superpowers/

# --- Merged from nodus/nsl/.gitignore (rete consolidation Task 4) ---
# grammar/node_modules re-rooted from nodus/nsl/.gitignore:1 — the ohm-js
# toolchain installed by the nodus/nsl README npm-install bootstrap.
/nodus/nsl/grammar/node_modules

# .pytest_cache/ was listed (unanchored) in both nodus/nsl/.gitignore and
# nodus/tests/.gitignore; kept unanchored here, matching the existing
# __pycache__/ convention above, so any future Python test tree is covered.
.pytest_cache/

# --- Merged from porta/.gitignore (rete consolidation Task 4) ---
# Re-rooted so patterns only match inside porta/, not repo-wide.
/porta/porta
/porta/cmd/porta/porta
/porta/**/*.db
/porta/**/*.db-shm
/porta/**/*.db-wal
/porta/**/build/
/porta/**/build-host/
/porta/**/.packages/
/porta/**/*.snapshot
/porta/**/*.bin
/porta/**/*.image
/porta/**/*.envelope
/porta/**/*.envelope.gz
/porta/nodus/host/image
/porta/nodus/host/image.crc32
/porta/nodus/host/firmware
/porta/**/*.log
/porta/deploy/dist/

# No /porta/CLAUDE.md rule here, deliberately (rete consolidation, IMPORTANT 3).
# porta's own .gitignore had `/CLAUDE.md`, so `git subtree add` correctly never
# imported it; re-rooting that line here would have made the file un-addable
# forever, and silently. That is the only reason the line is absent.
#
# It is NOT an instruction to add the file. Task 6 merges porta's rules into
# the ROOT CLAUDE.md and creates no porta/CLAUDE.md — one CLAUDE.md is the
# whole point of that task, and a second copy is a rule set that drifts.
# The rules must be read from ~/workspace/porta/CLAUDE.md (the only surviving
# copy) BEFORE Task 7 Step 2 deletes that clone.

# Tracked-build-artifact D-table names (not migrated into the monorepo history;
# see the rete consolidation design doc §4/D-table).
/porta/porta.db
/porta/porta-soak.log
/nodus/oevm/oevm_bench
/nodus/oevm/oevm_runner
